    "description": "The Emotional Regulation Questionnaire (ERQ) is a 10-item self-report scale measuring habitual use of two emotion-regulation strategies: cognitive reappraisal and expressive suppression. It is used in affective science and clinical research to examine individual differences in how people manage their emotional responses.",
